WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.642
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:14.659
Unit thirty-two: Both / Neither / Either / All. Today you will talk about two things or more than two things.

4
00:00:14.959 --> 00:00:17.600
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.894
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.426
Both.

7
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:26.114
Both means the two together.

8
00:00:26.717 --> 00:00:28.008
Both bags are new.

9
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:30.956
Your turn. Say: Both.

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.534
Both.

11
00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:36.087
Neither.

12
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:39.292
Neither means not one and not the other.

13
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:41.210
Neither bag is red.

14
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:43.947
Your turn. Say: Neither.

15
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.697
Neither.

16
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.161
Either.

17
00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.859
Either means one or the other.

18
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.730
Either bus is fine.

19
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:56.505
Your turn. Say: Either.

20
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:00.217
Either.

21
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:01.717
All.

22
00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:04.763
All means every one of three or more.

23
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.839
All students came.

24
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.742
Your turn. Say: All.

25
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.241
All.

26
00:01:13.983 --> 00:01:14.729
None.

27
00:01:15.717 --> 00:01:17.658
None means not one of three or more.

28
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.495
None of them came.

29
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.411
Your turn. Say: None.

30
00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.128
None.

31
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:27.803
Two things.

32
00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:31.327
Two things means used for both, neither, either.

33
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:32.941
Two things.

34
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.272
Your turn. Say: Two things.

35
00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.227
Two things.

36
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:42.042
More than two.

37
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:45.363
More than two means used for all and none.

38
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:46.998
More than two.

39
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:50.085
Your turn. Say: More than two.

40
00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:54.248
More than two.

41
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:55.984
Negative.

42
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.948
Negative means expressing no.

43
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.841
Neither is negative.

44
00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.358
Your turn. Say: Negative.

45
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.085
Negative.

46
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.342
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:16.170
Visal, compare two things you own using both and neither.

48
00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:24.977
Both my phones are old, but neither works well. Both and neither are for two things. Either means one of the two.

49
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.618
What are the grammar rules?

50
00:02:28.717 --> 00:02:41.705
Both takes a plural verb: Both are here. Neither and either take a singular verb: Neither is open. With of we need a plural noun or pronoun: both of them, neither of the shops.

51
00:02:42.817 --> 00:02:44.201
What about three or more?

52
00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:57.689
Use all and none: All the students passed. None of them was late. Neither already has a negative meaning, so do not add not: I like neither, not I don't like neither.

53
00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:00.392
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:05.281
Grammar focus: Both and neither and either and all and none.

55
00:03:05.581 --> 00:03:06.803
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.517 --> 00:03:09.272
Both my phones are old.

57
00:03:10.183 --> 00:03:11.730
Neither phone works well.

58
00:03:12.617 --> 00:03:14.558
All the students passed the test.

59
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:22.892
Both / neither / either = two things. All / none = three or more. Neither is already negative, so do not add 'not'.

60
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.011
Be careful! Don't say: Neither of them don't work.

61
00:03:28.967 --> 00:03:31.152
Say: Neither of them works.

62
00:03:31.452 --> 00:03:33.161
Neither is already negative.

63
00:03:33.967 --> 00:03:36.677
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.537
Two or More?.

65
00:03:38.837 --> 00:03:40.512
Both my phones are old.

66
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.896
Neither of them works well.

67
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.701
You can take either road because both lead to the town.

68
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.535
All the students in my class passed the test.

69
00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:52.836
None of them was late.

70
00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:57.900
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.645
blank of my parents drives. (both are non-drivers)

72
00:04:02.945 --> 00:04:05.936
A, Both. B, Neither. C, Either.

73
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.639
The answer is B: Neither.

74
00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:15.096
You can have tea or coffee. blank is fine.

75
00:04:15.396 --> 00:04:18.481
A, Either. B, Neither. C, Both.

76
00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.754
The answer is A: Either.

77
00:04:24.917 --> 00:04:27.952
blank the students passed. (all of 30)

78
00:04:28.252 --> 00:04:31.406
A, Both. B, All. C, Neither.

79
00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:37.129
The answer is B: All.

80
00:04:38.283 --> 00:04:39.528
Which is correct?

81
00:04:39.828 --> 00:04:44.654
A, I don't like neither.. B, I like neither.. C, I like not neither..

82
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.258
The answer is B: I like neither..

83
00:04:51.417 --> 00:04:54.241
According to the reading, how many roads lead to town?

84
00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:57.242
A, both. B, none. C, one.

85
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.544
The answer is A: both.

86
00:05:03.733 --> 00:05:06.688
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.235
Use 'both' and 'neither' to compare two things you own.

88
00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.922
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:21.222 --> 00:05:33.118
Both my phone and my laptop are old. Neither of them works very fast, but both are useful. I use both for two things and neither for a negative idea.

90
00:05:33.418 --> 00:05:35.302
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:36.217 --> 00:05:41.481
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and both and neither and either and all and none.

92
00:05:41.781 --> 00:05:45.664
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:05:45.964 --> 00:05:49.429
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:52.985
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

